// Network health for the Global Defensive perf overlay (one object, updated in place — read it every frame, no garbage):
//  rtt — the last pose request's network round trip (ms, as measured: not smoothed) · jitter — its variation (RFC 3550's
//  running mean of |Δrtt|, ms) · snapshotAgeMs — since the last state frame from the host (positions or combat) ·
//  interpMs — how far behind remote players are drawn (mean adaptive delay) · corrections / correctionMaxU — remote
//  bodies that jumped more than they can move in a frame (a snap, a late update pulled back; count, and the largest in game
//  units over the last 5 s; noteCorrection() adds the local player's own) · queue — requests in flight · hostTickMs — the
//  host's worst tick in the last second (its longest tick body, or how late a tick ran — a request or a long tick holding the
//  room's one thread shows here too) · lastSnapshotBytes — the last state frame's size.
