// spread of the offsets (t − arrival) over the window: a sample held 250 ms on Wi-Fi arrives with an offset 250 ms below the best — plus the
// sender's usual interval between two moving samples (ivl). A gap the SENDER chose (nothing changed: a player holding an angle, a mouse
// left still for a moment, a keep-alive every 2 s) moves t and arrival together, so it never counts. (v51 first counted arrival gaps
